{"answer":"Already demonstrated: the supplied historical records still support several bounded product atoms, only within their recorded boundaries. A directed tour-prerequisite structure passed five frozen isolated-SQLite cases. Prior-tour purchase eligibility passed seven installed cases with 324 assertions against controlled owner-derived SQLite fixtures. Search-payment evidence is historically reported as a controlled internal-service proof, not production payment verification, live discount eligibility, or checkout behavior. A usable 50% selector was historically reviewed as supported for deterministic selection or none, preservation of attributes and existing members, payment-usage guard execution, unchanged state, and promoted-path repetition; that still does not establish checkout installation or end-to-end checkout application.

The selfie-purchase-lookup atom remains demonstrated only as a bounded internal-service advance. Before that atom, RecognitionPurchaseEvidence exposed forMatches and forReference, but no forSelfie entrypoint; after it, RecognitionPurchaseEvidence::forSelfie was added and nine controlled actual-source executions validated the recorded match, ordering, duplicate, provider-failure, invalid-reference, and missing-history cases. The proof boundary remains controlled SQLite fixtures, intercepted provider HTTP, and direct service invocation. It is not checkout delivery, live same-person identity, prerequisite qualification, discount application, production deployment, or an autonomy gain.

Current baseline position has changed from “uninspected” to “bounded source-level research completed.” The recorded delivery baseline is still `taggable-server` branch `auto-50-perc-off` at prod commit `45826e12cdc8f585e514d7bb09c0d37fa28ed568`, and the new assessment inspected that committed tree. It also preserves an important boundary: the active worktree remained `feature/kiosk-square-return-recovery` with untracked files, so this was not execution from a checked-out delivery branch and not evidence of today’s live checkout.

The baseline research demonstrated that, within the inspected committed customer web path, the directed prerequisite storage/reader and named historical purchase-evidence services are missing, and the automatic 50% selector is missing from the baseline. It also identified reusable existing surfaces: recognition helpers and checkout supplied-code handling are present; checkout can read a redeem-code cookie, preview an entered or saved code, and save a discounted order during `postPayment` before provider handling. That existing supplied-code path does not establish prerequisite-based qualification or automatic discovery of a 50% code.

For machinery/provenance, the earlier input-interview and build-only atom-builder conclusions remain background, not product completion. Under the fixed goal record, the delivery goal is the Taggable automatic-discount product outcome; the historical machinery-development goal remains separate provenance rather than an additional completion condition for this product assessment.

Unfinished: the complete paid-prerequisite-purchase -> same-person recognition -> eligible current tour -> applicable existing 50% code -> discounted order before payment sequence is still not demonstrated. The assessment supports a first implementation boundary of restoring directed tour-prerequisite storage and reader on the prod-based branch, with checkout-tour/configured-pair inputs and prerequisite-ID outputs, but no restoration was executed. The inspected source still lacks the integrated qualification and automatic discovery/application connections, and there is no version-bound execution evidence of the full checkout sequence or preservation of surrounding checkout/search/payment behavior.

Still uncertain: executable reuse and dependency compatibility remain unverified; the packet reports historical proof-hash verification but zero fresh product tests, and current-dependency/MySQL compatibility remains outstanding. Recognition compatibility and purchase provenance remain unresolved because stored identifiers differ across recognition variants and purchase history can include fully discounted orders without payment. Live database state, AWS/recognition behavior, browser/payment/deployment behavior, configured discount codes, and whether the alternate kiosk API belongs to delivery scope remain untested or unresolved. Product completion remains unproved.","basis":[{"source_id":"goal","quote":"Deliver the agreed Taggable automatic 50% discount: at an eligible current-tour checkout, use the existing face-recognition flow to establish the same person’s paid purchase at any one configured prerequisite tour, locate an applicable existing 50% discount code, and apply it before payment. Keep the remaining checkout/search/payment behavior unchanged. Atom selection is the machinery choosing the work, not a competing development goal."},{"source_id":"goal","quote":"Delivery goal only. The historical machinery-development goal remains separate and unchanged."},{"source_id":"previous:tour-prerequisite-structure-historical-proof","quote":"Installed directed tour relationship migration and reader; all five frozen cases passed against installed source in isolated SQLite."},{"source_id":"previous:prior-tour-purchase-eligibility-historical-proof","quote":""installed_cases_passed": 7"},{"source_id":"previous:prior-tour-purchase-eligibility-historical-proof","quote":""installed_assertions": 324"},{"source_id":"previous:prior-tour-purchase-eligibility-historical-proof","quote":"Tests used controlled owner-derived SQLite fixtures."},{"source_id":"previous:search-payment-evidence-historical-review","quote":"This supports the internal service outcome, not production payment verification or discount eligibility."},{"source_id":"previous:usable-fifty-percent-selector-historical-review","quote":"deterministic selection or none, explicit exclusions, preserved attributes and existing members, actual verifier acceptance with matching record identity, payment usage guard execution, unchanged state, and promoted-path repetition."},{"source_id":"assessment:E0064","quote":"Current RecognitionPurchaseEvidence exposes forMatches and forReference, but no forSelfie entrypoint. A bounded app/routes search found no caller of RecognitionPurchaseEvidence. Nine current-baseline operator tests report available=false and no recognition request. Existing helper plus forMatches produces the recorded expected results in all nine cases."},{"source_id":"assessment:E0703","quote":"Baseline source and nine unavailable results establish the missing entrypoint; the after source and actual-source executions establish direct selfie-key lookup with complete recorded purchase evidence. This is an internal service capability demonstrated with controlled fixtures and intercepted provider HTTP, without checkout integration or identity decisions."},{"source_id":"assessment:E0706","quote":"All nine captured executions show the required request defaults, paid/unpaid and duplicate preservation, refusals, missing-history exception, unchanged dependencies and database. The recorded contribution-command failure remains a closeout limitation; this supports the bounded product outcome, not universal machinery reliability."},{"source_id":"previous:interview-live-acceptance","quote":"A fresh three-question interview replayed the actual clarification-control design change from this task."},{"source_id":"previous:interview-installed-proof","quote":""passed": true"},{"source_id":"previous:builder-decoupling","quote":"The installed atom builder accepts an owner-approved bounded atom without comparative selection."},{"source_id":"previous:builder-decoupling","quote":"Neither generates or r